  "term": "lactogenic hormone",
  "definition": "Lactogenic hormone is prolactin, a hormone released by the front part of the pituitary gland. It is mainly involved in milk production and, in some species, also affects reproduction, maternal behavior, fat metabolism, immune function, and the body’s water balance.",
